<title>SINGAPORE: Osprey to list in Singapore dollars.</title>
<headline>Osprey to list in Singapore dollars.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Osprey Maritime Ltd shares will be traded in Singapore dollars from December 20, said a statement from the Stock Exchange of Singapore on Monday.</p>
<p>Osprey is the first foreign company to get approval from the exchange to convert its US dollar listing to a Singapore dollar listing.</p>
<p>Singapore Finance Minister Richard Hu said in October that foreign companies listed in Singapore could convert to Singapore-dollar denominated stocks provided they met certain criteria.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
